[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Accepted: Early ...e5"]
[ECO "D24"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,hanging-piece"]
[Themes "win-a-pawn,knight-returns-to-c4"]
[Refutes "1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. e3 e5"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "for-us"]
[Opponent "4...e5"]
[Start "1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. e3"]

4... e5 $2 { Black tries to hit the centre at once, but the pawn on e5 is not defended by anything. } 5. Nxe5 $1 { Takes it. The pawn on d4 stays safe because the queen guards it, and the knight can step back to c4 to win the other pawn as well. } 5... Nbd7 6. Nxc4 { The knight comes back and takes the second pawn. White is a clean pawn up with a solid centre. } *
